Can you solve this antivirus puzzle challenge? 
You are given two PHP codes to scan a file using ClamAV and Avast anti-virus software. However, the detection rates of each anti-virus software are unknown. Can you calculate the detection rate (DR) for each software using the true positive (TP), false positive (FP), true negative (TN), and false negative (FN) values? Here's the formula to calculate DR in Latex:
\begin{equation}
DR = \frac{TP}{TP + FN}
\end{equation}
Can you use this formula to crack the puzzle and determine the DR values for ClamAV and Avast? Note that the resulting DR value is a percentage. Good luck!

