What steps do I need to follow in order to create a Java application that can implement an online survey to predict the respondent's level of personal happiness? The survey should cover factors such as social support, financial stability, work-life balance, physical health, and emotional wellbeing, as well as overall life satisfaction. The survey data should be stored in a [SQL database] for analysis. 
Can you provide an example of Java code that can be used to create the survey interface and store the data in a SQL database? Additionally, how can we ensure the accuracy and validity of the survey results through our code?
In terms of the code, we can start by creating a class for the survey questions and another class to handle the SQL database connections. We can also use HTML and CSS to create the survey interface. Here's an example of how the code might look like:
[Java code]
```java
// SurveyQuestions.java
public class SurveyQuestions {
    private String question;
    private int answer;
    public SurveyQuestions(String question) {
        this.question = question;
    }
    public String getQuestion() {
        return question;
    }
    public void setAnswer(int answer) {
        this.answer = answer;
    }
    public int getAnswer() {
        return answer;
    }
}
// SQLDatabase.java
import java.sql.*;
public class SQLDatabase {
    private Connection connection;
    private Statement statement;
    public SQLDatabase() {
        try {
            connection = DriverManager.getConnection("jdbc:mysql://localhost:3306/surveydata", "root", "");
            statement = connection.createStatement();
        } catch (SQLException e) {
            e.printStackTrace();
        }
    }
    public void addData(SurveyQuestions[] questions) {
        try {
            String query = "INSERT INTO surveydata (question, answer) VALUES (?, ?)";
            PreparedStatement preparedStatement = connection.prepareStatement(query);
            for (SurveyQuestions q : questions) {
                preparedStatement.setString(1, q.getQuestion());
                preparedStatement.setInt(2, q.getAnswer());
                preparedStatement.executeUpdate();
            }
        } catch (SQLException e) {
            e.printStackTrace();
        }
    }
    public void close() {
        try {
            statement.close();
            connection.close();
        } catch (SQLException e) {
            e.printStackTrace();
        }
    }
}
// Main.java
import java.util.Scanner;
public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        SurveyQuestions[] questions = new SurveyQuestions[5];
        questions[0] = new SurveyQuestions("How satisfied are you with your social support?");
        questions[1] = new SurveyQuestions("How stable is your financial situation?");
        questions[2] = new SurveyQuestions("How satisfied are you with your work-life balance?");
        questions[3] = new SurveyQuestions("How satisfied are you with your physical health?");
        questions[4] = new SurveyQuestions("How satisfied are you with your emotional wellbeing?");
        Scanner scanner = new Scanner(System.in);
        for (SurveyQuestions q : questions) {
            System.out.println(q.getQuestion());
            q.setAnswer(scanner.nextInt());
        }
        SQLDatabase db = new SQLDatabase();
        db.addData(questions);
        db.close();
    }
}
